  "body": "A threading insert carries one V width; there's no pitch range or partial-profile model.\n\n**Where:** the `Thread` kind takes one `width` + `tip_angle` (`crates/tools/src/tools.rs`, the Thread arm of `is_sane`).\n\n**Effect:** a common partial-profile 60° insert covering e.g. 48–8 TPI has to be stored at one pitch's width. The largest is the safe envelope, but it misstates the cutting profile at fine pitches, and the tool can't say which pitches it actually supports.\n\n**Fix sketch:** threading tools carry their form (partial or full profile, angle) and pitch range. The threading op refuses a pitch outside the range by name, and the envelope uses the profile at the cut pitch.\n\nEffort: high.\n\n**Done means:** one partial-profile insert serves its whole pitch range; a pitch outside it is refused by name; pinned.\n",
